WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.050
Charcoal is almost pure carbon.

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.930
Burn one kilogram of it on a barbecue,
and it seems to vanish into thin air.

3
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:13.330
Yet a calculation claims the fire makes
more than three kilograms of carbon dioxide.

4
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:19.130
Can burning one kilogram of charcoal really make
more than three kilograms of carbon dioxide?

5
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.950
In this mission, you'll read what a
balanced equation really tells you,

6
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.990
and write equations of your
own, state symbols included.

7
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.330
You'll learn three steps that solve
any reacting-quantity problem.

8
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.470
Your mission:

9
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.680
work out the mass of carbon dioxide
made from one kilogram of charcoal.
